From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 12:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: icc-bwmon: quiesce and drop the vote across sleep

The bwmon carries no PM ops: across a system suspend the monitor stays
enabled and its last interconnect vote stands. On SMD-RPM msm8998 the
vote is active-set only but the RPM never applies its sleep set, so a
standing vote holds DDR at the last measured rate for the whole
suspend. Disable the monitor and drop the OPP on suspend;
bwmon_start() reprograms everything from scratch on resume and the
first sample re-votes honestly. Validated across an 8-hour overnight
suspend.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/soc/qcom/icc-bwmon.c | 31 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/icc-bwmon.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/icc-bwmon.c
index 597f9025e422..66db83db3f2d 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/icc-bwmon.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/icc-bwmon.c
@@ -873,12 +873,43 @@ static const struct of_device_id bwmon_of_match[] = {
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, bwmon_of_match);
 
+static int bwmon_suspend(struct device *dev)
+{
+	struct icc_bwmon *bwmon = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+
+	/*
+	 * Quiesce the monitor and drop the interconnect vote.  On SMD-RPM
+	 * SoCs the vote is active-set only, but msm8998's RPM never applies
+	 * its sleep set (no APSS power-collapse handshake), so a vote left
+	 * standing here holds DDR at the last measured rate through the
+	 * whole system suspend.
+	 */
+	bwmon_disable(bwmon);
+	bwmon->target_kbps = 0;
+	bwmon->current_kbps = 0;
+
+	return dev_pm_opp_set_opp(dev, NULL);
+}
+
+static int bwmon_resume(struct device *dev)
+{
+	struct icc_bwmon *bwmon = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+
+	/* bwmon_start() reprograms the monitor from scratch. */
+	bwmon_start(bwmon);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static DEFINE_SIMPLE_DEV_PM_OPS(bwmon_pm_ops, bwmon_suspend, bwmon_resume);
+
 static struct platform_driver bwmon_driver = {
 	.probe = bwmon_probe,
 	.remove = bwmon_remove,
 	.driver = {
 		.name = "qcom-bwmon",
 		.of_match_table = bwmon_of_match,
+		.pm = pm_sleep_ptr(&bwmon_pm_ops),
 	},
 };
 module_platform_driver(bwmon_driver);
